{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"internal-chargeable-turtledove","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe src/rebar/_cli cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:28-52, 305-313, 442-462` — Preserve store-mount exclusions, pre-dispatch ordering, and one-snapshot invariant. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py:1-23, 56-62` — Preserve lexical pre-scan, any-position help, and `--` termination semantics. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_init.py:1-17, 55-69, 107-124, 189-212` — Preserve automatic attachment, explicit first-store consent, and best-effort mount boundaries. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py:1-20, 43-54` — Preserve configuration precedence and presence-only secret handling. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py:1-8, 59-109, 123-129, 162-167, 269-285, 321-445, 523-549` — Preserve current result/exit mappings, signing, and sidecar persistence. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/_common.py:1-26` — Preserve the distinction between CLI invalid-input errors and config defaulting. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_registry_checks.py:1-19, 32-47` — Preserve validation ownership and closed adapter/capability vocabularies. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py:1-17, 32-36, 415-448` — Preserve route authority, lazy resolution, aliases, and policy fields. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"0b6c-cf8e-a129-4e52","parent_id":"d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in src/rebar/_cli"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788570666375825464,"uuid":"b28434d6-73a3-451b-8218-00b04ec0e4db"}